This project (OOT: The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time on HarmonyOS) was made from a copy of NativeGames-harmonyos
(Tears of the Kingdom on HarmonyOS); the files it keeps from that project, changed or not (most of entry/ and of the
build scripts in native-harmonyos/), are under the same MIT terms, Copyright (c) 2026 NativeGames-harmonyos
contributors.

Files under native-harmonyos/overlay/ that have a counterpart in totk-android (at the commit in
native-harmonyos/UPSTREAM_PIN) are modified versions of those files and keep that project's MIT notice
(native-harmonyos/overlay/LICENSE.totk-android); the code under overlay/third_party/d2r_gfx/ started in d2r-mobile,
whose MIT notice is overlay/third_party/d2r_gfx/LICENSE. Of the overlay files without a counterpart,
runtime/ns2_host.c, ns2_codec.c, ns2_opus_ms.c, offline_host.c, audio_out_ohos.c and
third_party/d2r_gfx/gfx/nvn/nvn_ctl.h come from MacNativeGames (its MIT notice is the same text as totk-android's),
runtime/za_hle.c, za_shader_dump.c and game_patches_za.c from the LZA project, and the rest are this project's own;
several carry code ported from nxnative, and one part of ns2_host.c comes from pokopia-native, as their first
comments say.

Third-party code elsewhere (native-harmonyos/oot/d2r, native-harmonyos/third_party/dav1d,
native-harmonyos/third_party/etcpak) keeps its own license. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists all third-party code, here
and taken at build time.
